  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed first-floor side-to-rear extension in conjunction with the proposed roof extension to form end gable and additional two storey rear extension, and resultant terracing effect at the front elevation, would give rise to an unsympathetic, incongruous, bulky, obtrusive and contrived form of development which would fail to respect the scale, character, massing, composition and design of the host dwellinghouse and neighbouring properties. The proposal would therefore result in a detrimental impact to the character and appearance of the subject dwellinghouse and the visual amenities of the area, contrary to the high-quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), Policy GR1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021 – 2041), and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed first-floor extension at the side and rear elevations, by reason of the lack of significant setbacks at the side elevation and its excessive depth at the rear elevation, would breach the Council’s ‘45-Degree Code’ and give rise to overshadowing, loss of outlook, and an overbearing visual impact to the detriment of the residential and visual amenities of the occupiers of the neighbouring properties Nos. 49 and 53 Kenton Park Avenue. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), Policy GR1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021 – 2041), and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
